From 2eea97caf52bad97ffa99f0c8e704c71898d99b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: termux <termux@localhost>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] termuxgui: composite with OpenGL through a surfaceless EGL
 display

Without a DRM device the virtual backend only offers QPainter. When the
Termux:GUI integration is active and no DRM render device was found, create
a RenderDevice from EGL_MESA_platform_surfaceless (Zink, Panfrost, Turnip
... on top of the Android GPU stack) so that OpenGL compositing, effects and
the Qt Quick UI run on the GPU.

The new TermuxGuiEglBackend composites into a persistent render texture and
presents it into the Termux:GUI hardware buffers:
 - preferably by importing the buffer's dma-buf (fd 0 of its native handle,
   linear ABGR8888) through EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import and doing a GPU
   blit;
 - otherwise by glReadPixels() into a CPU mapping of the buffer.
Both paths keep compositing on the GPU; only the hand-over differs. If the
surfaceless display is unavailable or is a software renderer, everything
falls back to the existing QPainter backend unchanged.

RenderDevice::createVulkanDevice() is guarded against a null DrmDevice, and
the output-size handling of the QPainter backend is factored out so both
backends share it.

Knobs: KWIN_TERMUX_GUI_EGL=0 (force QPainter), KWIN_TERMUX_GUI_DMABUF=0
(force readback), KWIN_TERMUX_GUI_FLIP=0 (don't flip vertically),
KWIN_TERMUX_GUI_MODIFIER=<drm modifier> (override linear),
KWIN_TERMUX_GUI_ALLOW_SOFTWARE_GL=1 (accept llvmpipe & co).
